e  To handling the back to back ip_up_notifier in pppoe_service.OnPPPConnected, we have followed the following two approaches to fix this issue. 1) destroying the ppp_device_ instance before creating it again. This approach didnt work because ppp_device_ was registered with device_info. So this can only be destructed by shill manager and device_info. 2) another approach is by reusing the ppp_device_ instance but clearing the PPPDevice's connection_, ipconfig_ and selected_service_ fields. These fields will be created again with the newly received configuration. This approach has worked and provided the CL for review.  BUG=b:35774945 TEST=Tested on gale for the pppoe test cases with CDRouter.      Tested manually by stopping and starting the ppp server while its      already in pppoe connected mode.  Change-Id: I23179bc68028581c31a6bd51b361392348f9288f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/495949 Commit-Ready: Raju Konduru &lt;rkonduru@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Raju Konduru &lt;rkonduru@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="495949" owner_email="m.karthik@globaledgesoft.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/49/495949/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I21a39888360020d3cbc61cf09ceb0fca3eee335c" commit="423257e1557cf6d3e6e6609301cc1938f6df83e7" commit_message="cryptohome: Report migrated byte count and file count  BUG=chromium:714935 TEST=build  Change-Id: I21a39888360020d3cbc61cf09ceb0fca3eee335c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/512482 Commit-Ready: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Junichi Uekawa &lt;uekawa@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="512482" owner_email="hashimoto@chr